 won as White by 38 points. GPT-6.1 Sol was already behind early, then spent the middle game on the left edge, where moves 15 through 21 lost 6.8, 7.4, 11.8 and 17.2 points. After that the lead never came back, and later moves such as 37 H3 (20.0 points) widened it further. The 20k also gave away big swings, but always had enough left.", "moments": [{"turn": 9, "text": "D7 lost 5.1 points and dropped Black's lead from -3.1 to -8.1. The engine wanted E4, the centre point, and Black's stones drifted to the upper left instead."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "C5 lost 6.8 points, taking the lead from -5.0 to -11.7. The engine preferred B4, the point White took on the next move, so Black gave up the key spot on the left."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "A3 lost 11.8 points, from -12.0 to -23.8. On the board, Black crawls along the third line under White's row of stones on the fourth line, and White then plays E4 to close off the centre."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "B2 was the worst move of the early game at 17.2 points, sending the lead from -18.5 to -35.8. The engine's choice was G6, in the open centre. Black kept filling its own corner while the rest of the board was still unsettled."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "White's A1 lost 16.9 points, the biggest slip of the 20k's game, and the lead went from -35.8 back to -18.9. It was a rare chance, but Black's next move, E7, lost another 4.9 points and the chance passed."}, {"turn": 37, "text": "H3 was Black's biggest loss of the game at 20.0 points, from -20.1 to -40.0. The engine's choice was H5. White took H5 next and held the right side, and from there Black was playing for pride."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script only called the go play/board tools, parsed boards and counted groups and liberties (inspect117), kept logs, and replayed actual moves for verification (verify117, game-117-inspection.js); none looped over candidate moves or looked ahead, so the moves were chosen by the player.", "stop": fals